.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt EGGHEAD 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm egghead
.Nd concepts and architecture
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a record-store-first multi-agent system on Elixir/OTP. Plain
Markdown files are the substrate; agents are participants in the
graph, not owners of it. A SQLite index materializes queries over
the records. Agents are themselves records, with capabilities
declared in their frontmatter. External tools consult the whole
arrangement over MCP.
.Pp
Most multi-agent frameworks store their state in an internal
database and treat agents as the primary objects. The shape here is
inverted: the records survive the agents, the agents are staff for
the institution that the knowledge graph represents, and editing a
file is the deploy.
.Ss Records
A record is a Markdown
.Pq Pa .md
or org-mode
.Pq Pa .org
file in the records directory. The smallest record is one line of
Markdown; everything else
.Pq id, timestamps, author
has a sensible default. Optional YAML frontmatter declares structured
fields.
.Pp
A record's
.Sy class:
distinguishes its kind. Egghead recognizes:
.Bl -tag -width "deliberation" -compact
.It Sy durable
Long-lived knowledge. The default.
.It Sy inbox
Incoming, unprocessed.
.It Sy agent
An agent definition. The body is the system prompt.
.It Sy skill
A reusable instruction set.
.It Sy transcript
A saved chat-room transcript.
.It Sy deliberation
A distilled summary of an agent session.
.El
.Pp
Records can have tags, explicit frontmatter links, and wikilinks in
the body
.Pq Sy [[other-record]] .
The SQLite index provides FTS5 search, link traversal, and backlink
discovery; it is derived state, rebuildable from the source files at
any time.
.Ss Agents
An agent is a record with
.Sy class: agent .
The body of the record is the agent's system prompt; the frontmatter
declares the model, the tags, the capabilities, and a few
operational knobs (context threshold, max tokens, thinking).
.Pp
Drop a record with that class into the records directory and an
agent process starts. Edit it and the process hot-reloads. Delete it
and the process stops. There is no separate registration step, no
decorator, no role definition in a parallel file: the file is the
agent.
.Pp
A built-in agent named
.Sy index
is always available. It uses the model named in
.Sy default_model
and helps navigate the record store.
.Ss Chat rooms
A chat room is a long-lived process holding a shared transcript, a
roster of agents, and a turn budget. Every agent sees every message;
a coordinator decides which agents respond to each one based on how
the sender addressed it. Agents collaborate through the shared
transcript and self-select via
.Sy @-mentions ,
.Sy /pass ,
and tag-based relevance gating.
.Pp
Three dialogue modes:
.Bl -tag -width "@everyone" -compact
.It Sy open
Serial; agents may
.Sy /pass .
The default.
.It Sy @everyone
Huddle: serial, must-respond.
.It Sy @jam
Cacophony: parallel, low activation threshold.
.El
.Ss Capabilities and sandboxing
Authority is declarative. The
.Sy capabilities:
list in an agent's frontmatter enumerates exactly what verbs the
agent may perform. The shape is most directly inspired by OpenBSD's
.Xr pledge 2
and
.Xr unveil 2 :
the capability list is the
.Sy pledge
(what the agent can do), and the
.Sy in:
and
.Sy hosts:
scopes are the
.Sy unveil
(where it can do it).
.Pp
Resource families:
.Bl -column -compact "records " "read, create, update, delete"
.It Sy records  Ta read, create, update, delete
.It Sy agent    Ta create, update, delete, grant
.It Sy fs       Ta read, write, delete
.It Sy net      Ta get, post, put, delete
.It Sy proc     Ta exec (argv-style), eval (shell pipelines)
.El
.Pp
Internal verbs
.Pq Sy records.* , Sy agent.*
default to the universe in their bare form. External verbs
.Pq Sy net.* , Sy fs.* , Sy proc.*
default to empty in their bare form: an unscoped
.Sy net.get
grants nothing until you write down which hosts. Wide grants are
allowed; they have to be explicit.
.Pp
Two layers enforce capabilities:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
At every tool dispatch, the request is matched against the held
grants. Denials surface to the LLM, the transcript, and the log,
with a suggested YAML snippet that would widen the grant.
.It
For
.Sy fs.*
and
.Sy proc.*
verbs, the agent's subprocess is spawned inside an OS-level fence:
.Xr sandbox-exec 1
on macOS,
.Xr bwrap 1
on Linux. The sandbox is confined to the workspace declared in the
grant and severed from the network unless the grant opens it.
.El
.Pp
Widening a capability is always a human act
.Pq edit the record, or use Cm egghead agents grant .
Agents cannot grant capabilities they do not already hold; privileges
attenuate downward only. Capabilities written into a Markdown record
under Git turn each widening into a reviewable change.
.Ss Skills
A skill is a Markdown file pairing an instruction body with a
declaration of the tools that body assumes. The format follows the
.Lk https://agentskills.io "Agent Skills specification" .
Skills do not grant capabilities: a skill's
.Sy allowed-tools
is a
.Em requirement
the agent must already meet, not a grant. An agent that lacks the
required capabilities never sees the skill in its discovery list.
.Ss Tools and MCP
A tool is a function the model can call. The catalog merges three
sources:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Built-in tools (record-store operations, web fetch, filesystem,
subprocess).
.It
Tools registered from external MCP servers via
.Sy mcp_servers:
in the configuration. Each server's
.Sy requires:
declares the capabilities an agent must hold to be offered its tools.
.It
Tools provided directly by the LLM provider when the agent's model
supports them.
.El
.Pp
.Nm egghead
also exposes its own surface as an MCP server, with fifteen tools
covering record CRUD, graph traversal, agent prompting, and
ephemeral consultation. Two transports:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Cm Stdio
.Cm egghead mcp ,
JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout, used by editor integrations.
.It Cm HTTP
.Pa POST /mcp ,
mounted in the web router and available whenever
.Cm egghead serve
is running.
.El
.Ss Distribution
Every running
.Nm egghead
process is an Erlang node. When a second
.Nm egghead
command launches on the same machine, it discovers the long-running
.Cm egghead serve
over the local Erlang Port Mapper Daemon
.Pq epmd, TCP 4369 ,
connects, and becomes a client of that supervision tree. One set of
agents, one set of rooms, one record store. Same-host attach is
zero-config.
.Pp
The same mechanism extends to a LAN or a tailnet: set
.Sy server.host
in the configuration, copy
.Pa ~/.erlang.cookie
to peer hosts, and clients attach with
.Ev EGGHEAD_SERVER
or
.Fl -server .
BEAM distribution traffic is unencrypted on the wire and the
shared cookie is weak authentication; this is fine on a network that
authenticates connections itself, never safe on the public internet.
.Ss Architecture
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Egghead.Supervisor (one_for_one)
\(em\(em Phoenix.PubSub
\(em\(em RecordSupervisor (rest_for_one)
\(em   \(em\(em Index           \(em SQLite, derived & rebuildable
\(em   \(em\(em RecordStore     \(em file watcher, parser, write barrier
\(em\(em Agent.LayerSupervisor (rest_for_one)
    \(em\(em LLM.Registry     \(em multi-provider, env-var detection
    \(em\(em Chat.Coordinator \(em activation gating, /pass enforcement
    \(em\(em Agent.Supervisor (DynamicSupervisor)
        \(em\(em index          \(em built-in store agent
        \(em\(em agents/*       \(em records with class: agent
.Ed
.Pp
The record store is isolated from the agent layer. If the LLM
registry crashes and every agent restarts, search and traversal keep
serving. The clean record store outlives any individual session.
.Ss Design principles
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy Knowledge graph as institution
Records survive agents. Agents are staff, not the organization.
.It Sy Plain files are the universal interface
Markdown on a filesystem, not a database. Whatever already keeps
your notes safe is what keeps your store safe.
.It Sy Graph topology, sparse activation
Agents collaborate through a shared transcript and self-select via
.Sy @-mentions , Sy /pass ,
and tag-based relevance gating.
.It Sy Capability-based mutation control
Reads are free; writes follow a graduated spectrum enforced at the
infrastructure level, written into records and reviewable in Git.
.El
